What HJViewer says about itself, as decided on 2026-10-14:

- The maker is 프로젝트TF. Settings → About says so on a desktop and on a
  phone ("만든 곳: 프로젝트TF", "Made by 프로젝트TF"), and so do the HJViewer
  part of the copyright line on the desktop's About page and of the Windows
  version info (LegalCopyright of the Flutter runner, of the rustdesk crate
  and of the packer) and the runner's CompanyName. Upstream's copyright line
  stays as it is, as the AGPL asks.
- The pilot notice, in Korean and English like the account screens' other
  texts: "본 서비스는 현재 정식 서비스가 아니고 시범 구현이며, 예고 없이 변경될
  수 있습니다. 로그인은 현재 연세대학교 교직원만 대상으로 합니다." ("This service
  is not an official service yet. It is a pilot implementation and may change
  without notice. Login is currently available only to Yonsei University
  faculty and staff."). An account build shows it in a short line under the
  title of the login dialog, whose login goes to the Yonsei SSO, and in
  Settings → About.
- hjviewer.rs hides upstream's "Powered by RustDesk" link ("RustDesk 제공")
  in every build pinned to the hjviewer server, beside the other built-in
  settings it sets. Flutter's loadPowered (common.dart), which the desktop's
  home page and the phone's settings show, and the legacy UI already read
  hide-powered-by-me; apply() runs in the desktop processes
  (load_custom_client) and in the phone apps (flutter_ffi's initialize). A
  build without HJV_SERVER keeps upstream's link.

Hooks: one line each in login.dart, desktop_setting_page.dart and
settings_page.dart (hjvLoginPilot, hjvAboutNotice and hjvAboutNoticeTiles of
hjviewer_account.dart; the texts in hjviewer_account_texts.dart). Outside an
account build the login dialog stays as it was and About gains the maker's
line only.

Tests: hjviewer_account_test.dart holds both texts in both languages, the
About lines with and without an account build, and no braces in either.
The Windows version info, the login dialog, the About pages and the missing
link on each platform are checked on devices.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
